1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-4--4x-optional-situational-speaking","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-4/4x-optional-situational-speaking","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-4/4x-optional-situational-speaking","sourceHash":"2b9b0593ef6666075b5f6caf922136ca6089d6155a00f6f4b7271c4cedcc781c","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:55.737Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"4X (Optional) — Situational Speaking","zh":"4X（可选）——情境口语"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This is an optional sub-phase for learners who need to use the target language in specific real-life situations — living in a country that speaks the language, preparing for a trip, working in the language, or interacting with a local community.","zh":"这是一个可选的子阶段，适合需要在特定现实情境中使用目标语言的学习者——例如居住在使用该语言的国家、准备旅行、用这门语言工作，或与当地社区互动。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>It can be done at any point during or after Phase 4, or skipped entirely.</strong>","zh":"<strong>它可以在第4阶段期间或之后的任何时间进行，也可以完全跳过。</strong>"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The idea is simple: instead of general conversation practice, you focus on the specific situations you actually encounter (or expect to encounter) and make sure you have the vocabulary, phrases, and confidence to handle them.","zh":"理念很简单：不要练习泛泛的对话，而是专注于你实际遇到（或预计会遇到）的具体情境，确保自己拥有应对这些情境所需的词汇、短语和信心。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you're learning a language purely for enjoyment or long-term goals, you can skip this. But if you're about to move to a new country or you're already living there, this sub-phase can dramatically reduce daily frustration.","zh":"如果你学习一门语言纯粹是为了兴趣或长期目标，可以跳过这一阶段。但如果你即将搬到一个新国家，或者已经住在那里，这个子阶段可以显著减少日常生活中的挫败感。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"新增内容"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Phrase Memorization</strong> — Learning set phrases and expressions that are useful in specific situations. Unlike general vocabulary study, this is about memorizing ready-to-use chunks: greetings, common questions, polite requests, and the specific language of your target situations. These phrases act as building blocks you can rely on when your brain is too stressed to construct sentences from scratch. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/phrase-memorization\">Phrase Memorization</a>","zh":"<strong>短语记忆</strong>——学习在特定情境中有用的固定短语和表达。与一般的词汇学习不同，这里要记忆的是可以直接使用的语言块：问候语、常见问题、礼貌请求，以及目标情境中的特定表达。这些短语就像你可以依赖的积木，在大脑压力过大、无法从零组织句子时尤其有用。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/phrase-memorization\">短语记忆</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Domain-specific vocabulary</strong> — Targeted immersion and vocab study focused on the situations you're preparing for. If you're going to a hospital (hopefully for a wholesome reason), watch a medical drama. If you're enrolling your kid in school, read about education. The more specific and relevant your study, the more immediately useful it is. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/domains\">Domains</a>","zh":"<strong>领域特定词汇</strong>——围绕你正在准备的情境，进行有针对性的沉浸和词汇学习。如果你要去医院（希望是出于健康方面的好事），可以看医疗剧。如果你要给孩子办理入学，就阅读教育相关内容。学习内容越具体、越相关，就越能立即派上用场。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/domains\">领域</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Mad-libs Learning</strong> — A technique building on Phrase Memorization where you learn a sentence template and practice swapping in different words to create variations. For example, learning \"Could you please ___?\" and practicing it with dozens of different completions. This builds flexible, production-ready language from a small number of patterns. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/mad-libs-learning\">Mad-libs Learning</a>","zh":"<strong>填空式学习</strong>——一种建立在短语记忆之上的技巧：学习一个句子模板，然后练习替换不同的词语来创造变化。例如，学习“你能请你___吗？”并用几十种不同的补充内容进行练习。这能让你用少量句型构建灵活、可以直接产出的语言。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/mad-libs-learning\">填空式学习</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Topic Talk</strong> — Focused practice on specific topics or scenarios. The goal is to rehearse the vocabulary and phrases you want to be able to talk about. Best for people who live in a target language speaking country and want to build their social circle by going beyond small talk. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/topic-talk\">Topic Talk</a>","zh":"<strong>话题交流</strong>——针对特定话题或情境进行集中练习。目标是排练你希望能够谈论的词汇和短语。最适合居住在目标语言国家、希望通过超越寒暄来拓展社交圈的人。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/topic-talk\">话题交流</a>"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Balanced across all pillars with a heavy emphasis on output: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"各项支柱均衡分配，但重点放在输出上：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 20%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong>20%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 20%","zh":"<strong>互动式沉浸：</strong>20%"},{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Immersion:</strong> 20%","zh":"<strong>自由流沉浸：</strong>20%"},{"en":"<strong>Output:</strong> 40%","zh":"<strong>输出：</strong>40%"}]},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Vocab study (situation-specific): 20 mins","zh":"词汇学习（特定情境）：20分钟"},{"en":"Sentence Mining or flashcard creation: 20 mins","zh":"句子挖掘或制作闪卡：20分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Listening/Reading: 20 mins","zh":"自由流听力/阅读：20分钟"},{"en":"Tutoring session or Topic Talk: 40 mins","zh":"辅导课或话题交流：40分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This sub-phase is flexible. Some learners spend a few days on it, others a few weeks. Move on when you:","zh":"这个子阶段很灵活。有些学习者只花几天，另一些则花几周。满足以下条件后进入下一阶段："}},{"id":"segment-0018","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Know at least 50 words specific to your target situations","zh":"掌握至少50个与你的目标情境相关的词语"},{"en":"Have memorized 20+ useful phrases","zh":"记住20个以上的实用短语"},{"en":"Can handle the most common grammar patterns in your target situations without much hesitation","zh":"能够在目标情境中应对最常见的语法模式，且无需过多犹豫"}]}],"cards":[]}}]
